  {
    "Col_1": "",
    "Col_2": "False Positive",
    "Col_3": "State the status of the False Positive (FP). A FP occurs when a vulnerability is identified that does not actually exist on the system. This is known to happen from time-to-time with scanning tools. If the CSP believes a finding is an FP, the CSP must set this column to “Pending” and immediately submit a deviation request to their AO using the FedRAMP Deviation Request Form, including evidence of the FP. If the AO approves the deviation request, the CSP must change this to “Yes.” If the AO denies the deviation request, or if the CSP does not believe the finding is a FP, the CSP must set this entry to “No.” AO-approved False Positives can also be closed once these are validated by the 3PAO and approved by the AO. For further discussion regarding FPs and other POA&M topics, see The POA&M Template Completion Guide, available on the FedRAMP documents and Resources Webpage. (https://www.fedramp.gov/assets/resources/documents/CSP_POAM_Template_Completion_Guide.pdf)",
